From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Kulinich <entaytion@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:10:13 +0300
Subject: fix(entiny): keep wide channel post text inside the bubble

Long captions/messages on wide channel posts overflowed past the bubble
edge instead of staying within the wide width, and the side avatar slot
still reserved space it no longer needs in wide mode.

Thanks to exteraless (https://github.com/exteraless/exteraless) for the
original fix we ported this from (commit db2016b).

- gate the caption/text-overflow width recompute on isWideChannelPost()
  so long text no longer forces the bubble past the wide-post width
- add drawsSideAvatar() and use it in place of needDrawAvatar() for all
  side-avatar-dependent positioning (seek bar, buttons, background,
  overlays, poll buttons) so wide posts don't reserve avatar space
- drop the dead WIDE_FEED_POSTS/searchType==4 branch -- this fork has no
  Feed surface for it to apply to, so it was an unreachable toggle
